#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110295 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f67c3319-1153-51ed-a57a-f85c06c7e76c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear"}] :question/id #uuid "a042ba66-3567-5b06-84e6-344ad0043bbc" :question/math-academy-id "e-10748" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2f6d703c604c780da8c97a012b94e75f06a55aa8b6e706a1097dc33ff193e88c.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The points $K$, $N$, and $Z$ are collinear\n\nII. The points $K$, $P$, and $J$ are collinear" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/39/390f01ec8631f4c4eca0f391dd5b1c2f9e450e94d3bd992e6046c42dff0fc1e8.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/d9/d9d250f402d238388931ec077d17afe65b248d245ae6333f9cb150c18288ccce.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110296 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef4e321-841e-5933-b5e4-ff7dab6c5275" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid"}] :question/id #uuid "76902823-634d-5525-afc5-5f2a98cea481" :question/math-academy-id "e-10749" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams below shows three collinear points?\n\n![](images/c0/c0df27c96da9f9c285438faee93652f81362fe91a51dc28e02ec0e2e9ff42177.png)" :question/worked-solution "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/49/4967d8325f8ed8415a8404286d29ff97eb65cd6926ed1ca27a943178aee1a3cc.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/af/af746af6fba54f69570f5dcfa38fbbb4cffd290080cc45deec433bc5266aa75e.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/c0/c0d9d178c5be09aa7f6ad1927c6f8e930154cf077aabbd18a765820babd63069.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f67c3319-1153-51ed-a57a-f85c06c7e76c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09c250ea-692c-547e-a705-4dc418eb0270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441159} {:answer/id #uuid "2afe9ef2-fa5d-58e2-a13f-ad84913f8e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441164} {:answer/id #uuid "3e515ed7-b6fd-5000-9f48-7b91f5872c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441168} {:answer/id #uuid "49f84e6d-81e3-59eb-ace5-f4605b8b78c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441171} {:answer/id #uuid "4f1f1a9f-479e-59a1-8f7c-04625c06831d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09c250ea-692c-547e-a705-4dc418eb0270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441159} :answer-field/id #uuid "570bf11a-a7c8-574f-b3ff-0a5d67734d64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b615808c-9716-5264-afdc-7e0ca61bc6d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-13444" :question/problem "![](images/e9/e9ede3d8d40b90fcf4919b85917c2fa21bf91163d136a1cd40b8bd6c0db3b40d.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. Point $K$ is **not** collinear with the points $M$ and $N$\n\nII. Points $L,O,Q$ are collinear\n\nIII. Points $J,K,Q$ are **not** collinear" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/fa/fa3ac1e9323a72254ecfc2242b1de23c05f0cc639b593eeadacb64ed6b4d4036.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/88/8895800b4c1ca6d22d42fac0cdb1488f716bdb5b59b49496d2f908f0947314b0.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/f3/f39a0462a8a52762c7525e31746e69269ab4b9521f4cc4e8121b114e98ddb68a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f67c3319-1153-51ed-a57a-f85c06c7e76c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab463a2d-5905-58f7-af68-2bb4b2f11fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107322} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5b688b-0323-5661-8259-9b195cde3e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107323} {:answer/id #uuid "e27df00f-7404-5963-a875-5f57e801702e" :answer/type {:db/i