ing triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $Q,S,T$\n\nII. $M,O,Q$\n\nIII. $N,P,T$" :question/worked-solution "- $Q,S,T$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/21/2101dd8ae066aa55d601263de389e013100e476ddbf5220381e4040440b344a9.png)\n\n- $M,O,Q$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/d2/d29ca68ff7123964944eded292ec8ea2c6b16a9fd46e875472e7666f114c8cad.png)\n\n- $N,P,T$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/03/03db0865e93c7c9a1a2f1c23fd8027602e04299903edb6996b9f0b2150d1d036.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef4e321-841e-5933-b5e4-ff7dab6c5275" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2930bce2-2f13-5db1-a8f1-ab9025f0839b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441163} {:answer/id #uuid "7382d6a0-4b00-5760-8a3e-4d8d6f0ca1d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441174} {:answer/id #uuid "8d581c4b-9274-5fc9-ae38-3e7f3b141b4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441178} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b0219a-9bc0-59a1-8b26-dd203fc9aff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441192} {:answer/id #uuid "eea831b3-f18d-506b-b4af-052d9a45ea11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4b0219a-9bc0-59